\lispPackageChapter{candlesticks/data-retrievals}

A data retrieval is one act of fetching a set of data from a data source:
when it happened, the endpoint that was queried, and any notes.  Every
candlestick points back to the retrieval that produced it.

\section{Types}

\lispTypeSubsection{data-retrieval}

A CLOS class with slots \texttt{id}, \texttt{source-id},
\texttt{retrieved-at}, \texttt{endpoint}, and \texttt{notes}.  The
accessors are \lispId{data-retrieval-id},
\lispId{data-retrieval-source-id}, \lispId{data-retrieval-retrieved-at},
\lispId{data-retrieval-endpoint}, and \lispId{data-retrieval-notes}.
\texttt{retrieved-at} is a universal time.

\section{Functions}

\lispFunctionSubsection{record-retrieval}

Record that a set of data was retrieved from the data source with the
given \lispVar{source-id}, and return the new retrieval.
\texttt{:retrieved-at} is a universal time (default: now).
\texttt{:endpoint} and \texttt{:notes} are optional provenance details.

\lispSyntax

\lispCall{\texttt{(record-retrieval \lispVar{source-id} \&key \lispVar{retrieved-at} \lispVar{endpoint} \lispVar{notes})}}

\lispFunctionSubsection{retrieval-by-id}

The retrieval with the given \textsc{Uuid}, or \texttt{nil}.

\lispFunctionSubsection{data-retrieval-source}

The \texttt{data-source} that the retrieval came from.

\lispFunctionSubsection{data-retrieval-source-name}

The name of the data source that the retrieval came from.

\lispFunctionSubsection{retrievals-for-source}

The most recent retrievals from the data source with the given
\lispVar{source-id}, newest first.  \texttt{:limit} defaults to 100.

\lispSyntax

\lispCall{\texttt{(retrievals-for-source \lispVar{source-id} \&key \lispVar{limit})}}
